  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY NIGHT THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 1200 PM CST Sun Nov 8 2026\n\nThe above normal temperatures will continue on Tuesday as highs\nwarm into the around 70 degrees again around 10 degrees above\nnormal. \n\nAn upper level trough and a cold front will move through the\narea on Wednesday. There are some slight timing differences\nbetween the models but the front will be slowest to move \nthrough the eastern portions of the area where highs around 70 \nwill once again occur on Wednesday. Further east and north, highs\nin the middle to upper 60s will occur as the front passes \nthrough. The air mass right behind the front will be slightly \ncooler, a secondary upper level trough and front will move south\nthrough the region Wednesday night into Thursday bringing \ncooler temperatures to the area late week. \n\nA drier air mass will be in place and much of the area will \nlikely remain dry with the frontal passage on Wednesday but as \nthe front moves east slightly better forcing and moisture will \nresult in the potential for some showers and maybe a few rumbles\nof thunder east of Highway 65 on Wednesday. Additional light \nrain will be possible Wednesday night into Thursday with the \nupper level trough.\n\nA cooler air mas is expected to move into the area late week\nbehind the system. Highs in the upper 40s to the upper 50s are \nexpected Thursday and Friday. Lows in the 20s and 30s are \nexpected Friday and Saturday mornings.",
